message.content:
Looking at the test failures, the issue is in **fill-limit-3** and **f14-close-ack-2**: when the valve closes because accumulated volume reaches target, `doneSensor` is already `TRUE`, but the confirmation doesn't happen in the same scan. The code transitions to state 2, and only checks `doneSensor` on the **next scan**.

The public requirement states: "本拍关阀后立即读取 doneSensor" - meaning we must check `doneSensor` **immediately** when the valve closes, not on a subsequent scan.

```json
{"edits":[{"old":"        1: // filling
            tmp_accVol := tmp_accVol + flowVol;
            IF tmp_accVol >= targetVol THEN
                valveOpen := FALSE;
                tmp_pending := TRUE;
                state := 2;
            END_IF;", "new":"        1: // filling
            tmp_accVol := tmp_accVol + flowVol;
            IF tmp_accVol >= targetVol THEN
                IF doneSensor THEN
                    IF fillsToday < 32767 THEN
                        fillsToday := fillsToday + 1;
                    END_IF;
                    tmp_pending := FALSE;
                    valveOpen := FALSE;
                    state := 0;
                ELSE
                    valveOpen := FALSE;
                    tmp_pending := TRUE;
                    state := 2;
                END_IF;
            END_IF;"}, {"old":"        2: // pendingConfirm
            IF tmp_risingStart THEN
                IF tmp_pending THEN
                    tmp_pending := FALSE;
                END_IF;
                tmp_accVol := flowVol;
                IF flowVol >= targetVol THEN
                    valveOpen := FALSE;
                    tmp_pending := TRUE;
                ELSE
                    valveOpen := TRUE;
                    state := 1;
                END_IF;
            ELSIF doneSensor THEN", "new":"        2: // pendingConfirm
            IF tmp_risingStart THEN
                IF doneSensor THEN
                    IF fillsToday < 32767 THEN
                        fillsToday := fillsToday + 1;
                    END_IF;
                    tmp_pending := FALSE;
                END_IF;
                tmp_accVol := flowVol;
                IF flowVol >= targetVol THEN
                    valveOpen := FALSE;
                    tmp_pending := TRUE;
                ELSE
                    valveOpen := TRUE;
                    state := 1;
                END_IF;
            ELSIF doneSensor THEN"}]}
```
